{
  "$comment": [
    "Industry taxonomy slug -> Overture Places categories (ADR-0017).",
    "",
    "Why this file exists, measured on the Delhi box (269,309 businesses): passing our",
    "`googleTypes` straight to Overture reached 12.1% of them and matching Overture's own leaf",
    "category reached 16.1%, because Overture names things differently -- it has no `car_repair`,",
    "no `university`, no `physiotherapist` and no `bicycle_store`. With this mapping, 96.2%.",
    "",
    "A match tests every level of a place's hierarchy, so mapping to the right level is the whole",
    "job. Too specific and most of the category is missed. Too broad and the request stops meaning",
    "anything: `fashion_and_apparel_store` looks like the obvious parent for a clothing shop until",
    "you see that it also holds jewelry_store, shoe_store and eyewear_store, and `laundry_service`",
    "sits under `services_and_business` with 1.2 million other things. Widening is a judgement per",
    "category, never a rule.",
    "",
    "Sectors are mapped as well as categories, to Overture's broad parents. A place whose only",
    "category is `professional_service` has no leaf to match, and there are 5,731 of them in Delhi",
    "alone; without the sector rows they were unreachable by any request. Asking for a sector is",
    "also what a user does when they say \"shops in Gurgaon\" rather than naming a trade.",
    "",
    "An empty list means Overture has no category for this and is not a gap to paper over: the",
    "connector falls back to searching names inside the area, which is honest about being less",
    "precise. Mapping `tuition-centre` to `home_service` because a tokeniser suggested it would",
    "be worse than nothing.",
    "",
    "Categories are verified against db/seeds/data/overture-categories-in.json by a test; a",
    "category Overture does not publish fails the build rather than silently matching nothing."
  ],
